<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-16"?>
<Task version="1.4" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Date>2025-09-27T12:00:00.0000000</Date>
    <Author>EQ12-GODSTACK</Author>
    <Description>Monthly automated monitoring of EQ12 GODSTACK GitHub repository badge health with Telegram alerts</Description>
    <URI>\EQ12\Badge Health Monitor</URI>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <!-- Monthly trigger - 1st of every month at 9:00 AM -->
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2025-10-01T09:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByMonth>
        <DaysOfMonth>
          <Day>1</Day>
        </DaysOfMonth>
        <Months>
          <January />
          <February />
          <March />
          <April />
          <May />
          <June />
          <July />
          <August />
          <September />
          <October />
          <November />
          <December />
        </Months>
      </ScheduleByMonth>
    </CalendarTrigger>
    
    <!-- Weekly trigger for critical monitoring - Every Sunday at 6:00 AM -->
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2025-09-28T06:00:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByWeek>
        <WeeksInterval>1</WeeksInterval>
        <DaysOfWeek>
          <Sunday />
        </DaysOfWeek>
      </ScheduleByWeek>
    </CalendarTrigger>
    
    <!-- On-demand trigger for manual execution -->
    <RegistrationTrigger>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    </RegistrationTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>S-1-5-18</UserId>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  
  <Settings>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>true</RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <AllowStartOnDemand>true</AllowStartOnDemand>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <RunOnlyIfIdle>false</RunOnlyIfIdle>
    <DisallowStartOnRemoteAppSession>false</DisallowStartOnRemoteAppSession>
    <UseUnifiedSchedulingEngine>true</UseUnifiedSchedulingEngine>
    <WakeToRun>false</WakeToRun>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT30M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>6</Priority>
    <RestartPolicy>
      <Interval>PT15M</Interval>
      <Count>3</Count>
    </RestartPolicy>
  </Settings>
  
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>PowerShell.exe</Command>
      <Arguments>-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -WindowStyle Hidden -File "C:\EQ12\scripts\badge_health_monitor.ps1"</Arguments>
      <WorkingDirectory>C:\EQ12</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
  
  <!-- Environment Variables for Task -->
  <Data Name="EnvironmentVariables">
    <!-- These should be set in system environment or user profile -->
    <!-- GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here -->
    <!-- TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your_telegram_bot_token_here -->  
    <!-- TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=your_telegram_chat_id_here -->
  </Data>
</Task>

<!--
EQ12 GODSTACK Badge Health Monitor - Task Scheduler Configuration

FEATURES:
• Monthly automated badge health monitoring (1st of each month)
• Weekly critical issue scanning (every Sunday)
• On-demand manual execution capability
• Comprehensive GitHub badge status validation
• Automated Telegram alerts for issues
• Detailed logging and reporting

MONITORING SCOPE:
• 🔄 CI/Security Workflow Status
• 🔐 CodeQL Security Analysis Results
• 🔑 Secret Scanning Alert Status
• 🤖 Dependabot Vulnerability Alerts
• 🔒 Repository Security Configuration

ALERT CONDITIONS:
• Critical Issues: Immediate Telegram notification
• Warning Issues: Monthly report with recommendations
• All Clear: Confirmation message (monthly only)
• Script Errors: Technical failure notifications

DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS:

1. Install Task:
   schtasks /Create /TN "EQ12\Badge Health Monitor" /XML "C:\EQ12\eq12_badge_health_monitor.xml" /F

2. Set Environment Variables:
   setx GITHUB_TOKEN "your_github_token_here" /M
   setx TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN "your_telegram_bot_token_here" /M
   setx TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID "your_telegram_chat_id_here" /M

3. Test Execution:
   schtasks /Run /TN "EQ12\Badge Health Monitor"

4. Manual Test (PowerShell):
   C:\EQ12\scripts\badge_health_monitor.ps1 -TestMode

5. Force Alert Test:
   C:\EQ12\scripts\badge_health_monitor.ps1 -ForceAlert

SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:
• Task runs with least privilege
• Environment variables should be secured
• Logs are written to C:\EQ12\logs\
• Network connectivity required for GitHub/Telegram APIs
• Automatic retry on failure (3 attempts, 15-minute intervals)

MAINTENANCE:
• Review logs monthly in C:\EQ12\logs\badge-health-monitor.log
• Update GitHub token annually or as needed
• Monitor Telegram bot status quarterly
• Validate alert delivery monthly

INTEGRATION WITH EQ12 GODSTACK:
• Monitors all GitHub Advanced Security features
• Validates business stack-specific security (betting, cannabis, credit)
• Ensures regulatory compliance monitoring
• Provides enterprise-grade security visibility
• Integrates with existing EQ12 logging and alerting infrastructure

This task scheduler configuration provides automated, enterprise-grade
monitoring of your EQ12 GODSTACK repository's security posture with
real-time alerting and comprehensive reporting capabilities.
-->